WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.260 --> 00:00:01.260
Hi, guys.

00:00:01.260 --> 00:00:02.260
Dr. Berg here.

00:00:02.260 --> 00:00:06.120
In this video we're going to talk about insulin
resistance, potassium, and blood pressure.

00:00:06.120 --> 00:00:13.440
Out of all the nutrients that you need, potassium
is something needed in very large quantities.

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:18.470
You need 4700 mg of potassium every single
day.

00:00:18.470 --> 00:00:20.400
What does that mean with food?

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:25.160
It means that hardly anyone is getting their
potassium, because you would need 7 - 10 cup

00:00:25.160 --> 00:00:27.500
of vegetables every single day.

00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:30.740
How many cups of vegetables do you consume
in given day?

00:00:30.740 --> 00:00:32.410
Maybe five?

00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:34.010
Maybe less?

00:00:34.010 --> 00:00:37.719
I do it because I feel so much different.

00:00:37.719 --> 00:00:38.879
Here's the thing.

00:00:38.879 --> 00:00:43.979
We need four times as much potassium as we
do sodium.

00:00:43.979 --> 00:00:48.260
Most people consume four times as much sodium
as they do potassium and they have a lot of

00:00:48.260 --> 00:00:49.260
fluid retention.

00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:55.159
So, they both work together in relationship
to fluids and hydration.

00:00:55.159 --> 00:00:59.989
If you look at vegetable content, it's always
heavy on the potassium and very low on the

00:00:59.989 --> 00:01:05.690
sodium, but if you're doing chips and salty
things, that's going to throw this whole thing

00:01:05.690 --> 00:01:06.860
off.

00:01:06.860 --> 00:01:11.550
What happens when you have low potassium is
you get high blood pressure.

00:01:11.550 --> 00:01:12.850
Potassium is a physiological relaxer.

00:01:12.850 --> 00:01:15.190
It calms the nervous system.

00:01:15.190 --> 00:01:18.300
It actually softens the arteries.

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:19.830
It actually can prevent strokes.

00:01:19.830 --> 00:01:21.800
It's very, very healthy.

00:01:21.800 --> 00:01:23.010
Healthy mineral.

00:01:23.010 --> 00:01:26.500
It can also prevent constipation.

00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:30.050
It also can prevent leg cramps.

00:01:30.050 --> 00:01:36.480
It's involved in nerve conductivity and muscle
contraction and relaxation.

00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:40.640
With a problem with potassium you can have
a lot of cramps, tightness, and tension in

00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:46.060
your body and you can also have a lot of electrical
problems with your heart.

00:01:46.060 --> 00:01:52.480
Arrhythmias, atrial fib, that's all potassium
deficiency because people don't consume enough.

00:01:52.480 --> 00:01:56.520
Let's pretend you have high blood pressure
and you have to take a diuretic thiazide.

00:01:56.520 --> 00:02:00.820
Well, what that does is it gets rid of fluid.

00:02:00.820 --> 00:02:07.050
Well, it also gets rid of potassium, so what
happens when you take this diuretic to fix

00:02:07.050 --> 00:02:12.700
your high blood pressure, you lose more potassium
raising the blood pressure more.

00:02:12.700 --> 00:02:15.830
So, now you need another medication.

00:02:15.830 --> 00:02:21.120
And then you're told to drink more water,
which dilutes the electrolytes more, especially

00:02:21.120 --> 00:02:26.810
potassium, and your blood pressure goes higher,
because more water is not going to hydrate

00:02:26.810 --> 00:02:27.810
you.

00:02:27.810 --> 00:02:31.700
It's going to get rid of the electrolytes
that you have, potassium specifically, and

00:02:31.700 --> 00:02:33.329
you don't get the hydration you once had.

00:02:33.329 --> 00:02:37.930
So the whole myth of drinking more water to
hydrate you is not quite true.

00:02:37.930 --> 00:02:41.129
You need the minerals, specifically potassium.

00:02:41.129 --> 00:02:42.920
That's the one you need in the most amount.

00:02:42.920 --> 00:02:50.739
Even magnesium, you need about 420 mg, but
potassium you need 4700.

00:02:50.739 --> 00:02:56.739
Also, if you're salt sensitive, especially
with your blood pressure, what that really

00:02:56.739 --> 00:02:59.709
means is you're potassium deficient.

00:02:59.709 --> 00:03:04.440
The way to fix people that are salt sensitive
is just increase the potassium and they'll

00:03:04.440 --> 00:03:05.440
do fine.

00:03:05.440 --> 00:03:08.549
Instead of restricting salt, why don't we
just increase potassium?

00:03:08.549 --> 00:03:13.260
It's a better strategy because you need potassium
for other things.

00:03:13.260 --> 00:03:21.340
98% of all the potassium in your body is inside
the cell, not outside the cell.

00:03:21.340 --> 00:03:27.419
When you get tested from your blood or whatever
testing you do, it's very difficult to test

00:03:27.419 --> 00:03:32.219
a potassium deficiency because it's all inside
the cell.

00:03:32.219 --> 00:03:37.590
You might think you have normal levels, but
you really don't because you never did an

00:03:37.590 --> 00:03:41.090
intracellular test for potassium.

00:03:41.090 --> 00:03:48.680
The other interesting thing about potassium
is it takes insulin to control and absorb

00:03:48.680 --> 00:03:50.819
potassium.

00:03:50.819 --> 00:03:56.969
If you don't have enough insulin, you can't
pull potassium in the cells.

00:03:56.969 --> 00:03:59.819
Insulin regulates potassium.

00:03:59.819 --> 00:04:05.569
How does that relate to a pre-diabetic, someone
has insulin resistance or diabetic?

00:04:05.569 --> 00:04:10.799
Well, if they have insulin resistance, the
cells are going to block insulin.

00:04:10.799 --> 00:04:13.220
So guess what's going to happen to the potassium?

00:04:13.220 --> 00:04:17.070
They're not going to have enough potassium.

00:04:17.070 --> 00:04:22.161
A lot of times when you have a pre-diabetic
or even a diabetic state, they have a huge,

00:04:22.161 --> 00:04:25.950
huge deficiency of potassium.

00:04:25.950 --> 00:04:31.390
One of the things I make sure that they do
is greatly increase the vegetable content

00:04:31.390 --> 00:04:37.600
to increase the potassium to help balance
this thing out because they're going to have

00:04:37.600 --> 00:04:39.700
so many side effects from that.

00:04:39.700 --> 00:04:44.370
If you actually add more potassium you can
decrease the need for insulin.

00:04:44.370 --> 00:04:45.530
That's a really cool relationship.

00:04:45.530 --> 00:04:51.340
I just wanted to touch on the relationship
between these three items right here.

